anding in a  deeply memorable moment Zorro offers up  his life in exchange for Luffy's even  going down on his knees and giving up on  his dream of becoming the greatest  swordsman the deal with humor means  taking on all the pain in Luffy's  battered body staying true to his  Bushido code Zoro asks Kuma to change  locations so no one can witness his  sacrifice stoic steadfast and courageous  to a fault when Sanji later finds him  alive but standing in a massive radius  of splattered blood Zora replies nothing  happened this moment will live on in the  history of One Piece as the most  honorable Act of any crew  anymore  we're entering the big league now and at  number two we have Zorro stopping big  mom and kaido's combined attack  onigashima  the conclusive battle Atop The Skull  Dome sees Zorro Luffy your kid and  killer go up against the two most feared  and Powerful Pirates of their time the  yonko duo clearly don't think too much  of their challenges and aim to bring  them down in a single shot with zero  hope of dodging the attack the rookies  can only watch in horror as the  atmosphere around them crackles that is  until Zorro without a Thor for himself  steps in front of his allies and blocks  the massive blast deflecting it upwards  and sacrificing himself a firm believer  of the samurai code of facing attacks  head on sorrow never flinches even in  the face of his imminent death having  come a long way since joining Luffy  Zorro has never shown weakness from the  very beginning and he's always had his  captains back as we saw in the episode  with Kuma  [Applause]  if blocking the yonko's attack on his  own wasn't enough Zorro slashes kaido  and gives him a scar to remember for our  top pick today  [Applause]  once again stepping in to protect his  captain The Swordsman makes a valiant  effort to Gold kaido into finishing him  off first having already sustained  serious injuries from kaido and big  mom's attacks earlier he makes one last  stand against the